      "message": "The uuid comes from socket_info, which is only created from `make_l2cap_channel` or `make_rfcomm_channel`. For l2cap, the uuid is none which is blocked in and_then function. For rfcomm, the uuid should be protected by the complex dbus macro and be only valid if it success in try_from[1]. So I think the uuid shouldn\u0027t be empty here.\n\n\n[1]https://source.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/aosp/packages/modules/Bluetooth/upstream/system/gd/rust/topshim/src/btif.rs;l\u003d369?q\u003dsystem%2Fgd%2Frust%2Ftopshim%2Fsrc%2Fbtif.rs\u0026ss\u003dpiper%2FGoogle%2Fchromeos_public:src%2Faosp%2Fpackages%2Fmodules%2FBluetooth%2Fupstream%2F",
